<section class="wp-block-group alignfull ok-body"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-lede"} -->
<p class="ok-lede">Okami College was founded in Lisbon in 2009 to teach hotel management on an operational floor rather than in an ordinary lecture hall. We prepare students for hospitality careers through daily service inside our own teaching hotel.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:group {"className":"ok-col","layout":{"type":"default"}} -->
<div class="wp-block-group ok-col"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Founded on the Floor in Lisbon</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Okami College was established in 2009 by experienced hotel practitioners in Lisbon, Portugal. The founders recognized that conventional classroom study could never replicate the pressure, timing, and interpersonal nuance of a working hotel floor. Rather than relying on simulated desks and abstract case studies, the college established its campus and teaching hotel at Rua do Farol 22, 1200-180 Lisboa. From our very first intake, we committed to training small cohorts under the direct supervision of career hoteliers. Today, that founding principle remains unchanged across every department. Students learn how a property breathes, from morning arrivals and room turnarounds to evening banquet service, by taking responsibility for genuine operations day after day.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">Why the College Operates Okami House</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">We operate Okami House because true hospitality standards cannot be mastered from a textbook. Okami House is a fully functioning teaching hotel featuring forty-two guest rooms, a sixty-cover restaurant, and a dedicated banquet room open to paying public guests. When students check in an arrival, serve a lunch table, or prepare a guest room, the expectations and consequences are entirely genuine. Instructors stand alongside students on the floor, observing technique, correcting posture, and guiding guest conversations in real time. This operational immersion ensures that professional habits become second nature long before students begin their industry placements, building unshakeable competence in real service environments.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":2,"className":"ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h"} -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading ok-h2 ok-h2--left ok-col__h">How Our Instructors Are Chosen</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"ok-copy"} -->
<p class="ok-copy">Every instructor at Okami College is chosen first for substantial floor leadership in demanding hotels, and second for the ability to mentor young professionals. Our faculty members have spent decades managing front desks, coordinating high-volume banquets, and leading professional kitchen brigades across international properties. They understand the exact operational standards that reputable general managers expect from supervisors. Because our instructors have lived the realities of hotel shifts, they teach practical workflows, calm problem-solving, and meticulous attention to detail rather than detached theory. Students are treated as junior colleagues on the floor, receiving continuous feedback that reflects the highest standards of contemporary hotel operations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
